      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n5. Section 451 and 457 of CrPC, 1973 is reproduced hereunder for ready reference:-\n\"451. Order for custody and disposal of property pending trial in certain cases.--When any property is produced before any Criminal Court during any inquiry"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e0c141ed7b924fe9908fe7c83a37450a_12",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "the purposes of this section"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7b9aebeceb5248b99355730a79adb6f2_13",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": ", \"property\" includes-- (a) property of any kind or document which is produced before the Court or which is in its custody; (b) any property regarding which an offence appears to have been committed or which appears to have been used for th"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "572c16b238e7481484d29bcfeef278eb_14",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n457. Procedure by police upon seizure of property.--(1) Whenever the seizure of property by any police officer is reported to a Magistrate Page No.# 3/4 under the provisions of this Code, and such property is not produced before a Criminal"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "759de0d75b394cb0a84bcb01a021c8a8_15",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(2) If the person so entitled is known, the Magistrate may order the property to be delivered to him on such conditions (if any) as the Magistrate thinks fit and if such person is unknown, the Magistrate may detain it and shall, in such cas"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "405f1ae1007a4c41980c3021463c9c71_16",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n6. The Apex Court in the case of Sunderbhai Ambalal Desai vs State of Gujarat reported in (2002) 10 SCC 283, while dealing with disposal of seized materials irrespective of whether it is an application under Section 451 or an application u"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7ce309fb6eb340c59b6dc080d93336c8_17",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That the application for zimma of seized material shall be dealt expeditiously and judiciously with the object that the owner of the seized article should not suffer for it being remaining unused or by its misappropriation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bf58cabf98a8432f88a7e26b0addca83_18",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nB. Whatever the situation be, it is of no use to keep the seized materials at police station for a long period."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b31b3a7e47134edeaa00fe43ce6b8c00_19",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAzhar Hussain vs The State Of Assam on 28 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/83183375/\n2 C."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3b8d2883f0d24fb18023a36991486bf6_20",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If proper panchnama before handing over possession of the article is prepared,\nthat can be used in evidence instead of it production before Court during trial."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0db24e6b201749ebbf9ffdd303a7e84d_21",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nD. To protect the interest of the investigation/trial, the seized article can be handed over to the applicant by preparing detail and proper panchnama of such article,\ntaking photographs of such article and a bond that such article would b"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4d9b1d54460b47c2a7872e1cf76ffcf8_22",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Court for this Page No.# 4/4 purpose,\nmay take proper security also."
    },
    {
